Changelog: 02-11-2026 00:06:22

Added. The picture full screen (owner, 01-11-2026): A on the Picture card starts it in the whole window, with its
buttons in the row at the bottom. A Screenshot saves what shows as a PNG in the Pictures folder, X Record starts a
recording of what shows and X Stop ends it (an MP4, H.264 through Windows' own encoder, at the mode's size and at most
30 frames a second, in the Videos folder; both in a USB HD Cam folder, named with the date and the time), Y Gray and
Y Color switch to black and white and back (remembered), LT Zoom − and RT Zoom + zoom from 1x to 4x, and the d-pad,
the left stick or a finger moves the zoomed picture (the mouse wheel zooms). LB Mode − and RB Mode + change the mode
there too, not while it records. B ends the full screen; a recording stops and is kept, and View asks for a second
press while one runs. If the camera stops sending, the full screen says why and stays, so another mode can be tried.
The line above the row shows the mode, the zoom and the recording's time. Signs and short words in the row, so its ten
entries fit at 1280 x 720 (measured by a test in every state). New: record.py, preview.Look and shown(), the panes'
FullPicture, with tests, among them a real recording read back.

